<Doc title="Guide for AI agents · Are we ARM yet?" description="How an AI agent helps an ARM laptop's owner check what works under Linux, report it to arewearmyet.com and propose fixes to Omarchy." plain="/agents.md">
  <div slot="top" class="mt-8 rounded-xl bg-[#9ece6a]/10 p-5 text-sm text-zinc-300 ring-1 ring-[#9ece6a]/40">
    Working with an AI agent on your laptop? Tell it: <code class="rounded bg-zinc-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-100">Read https://arewearmyet.com/agents.md and help me check this laptop.</code> The same guide is below, for you to read what it will do. It sends what it finds to arewearmyet.com, without serial numbers, addresses or names, opens pull requests on Omarchy for what it fixes, and tries kernel and device tree changes from boot entries of their own, restarting and picking up again as it needs. It keeps your working boot entry, never touches your files or disk, and asks before posting anywhere else.
